---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import VectorsTable from '../components/VectorsTable.astro';
import FeedbackWidget from '../components/FeedbackWidget.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const toc = [
  { id: 'how', text: '1. How to Run the Vectors' },
  { id: 'valid', text: '2. Valid Runestones (V1–V8)' },
  { id: 'cenotaph-vectors', text: '3. Cenotaph Vectors (C1–C14)' },
  { id: 'non-runestone', text: '4. Non-Runestone Outputs (N1–N2)' },
  { id: 'ignored', text: '5. Ignored Values & Edge Cases' },
  { id: 'beyond', text: '6. Beyond the Payload' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Runes Test Vectors"
  description="Authoritative conformance test suite containing all 24 vectors (V1–V8, C1–C14, N1–N2) verified against ord 0.29.0."
  currentRoute="vectors.html"
  kicker="Protocol Conformance Suite"
  toc={toc}
>
  <div class="status-line">
    24 authoritative test vectors verified against Casey Rodarmor's ord 0.29.0 reference test suite.
  </div>

  <h2 id="how">1. How to Run the Vectors</h2>
  <p>
    You can run this test suite in your browser, via the command line, or in automated CI:
  </p>
  <pre><code># Run vectors via local CLI
npm run test:conformance

# Or run via @bitcoinuniverse/runes-tools CLI
npx runes run-vectors --json</code></pre>
  <p>
    You can also test any vector interactively in the browser by clicking the <strong>Test →</strong> button next to each vector below, or in the <a href={`${base}/conformance.html`}>Conformance Center</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="valid">2. Valid Runestones (V1–V8)</h2>
  <p>
    These vectors represent valid runestones that parse without flaws under consensus rules.
  </p>
  <VectorsTable category="valid" caption="Valid Runestones (V1 through V8)" />

  <h2 id="cenotaph-vectors">3. Cenotaph Vectors (C1–C14)</h2>
  <p>
    These vectors demonstrate malformed or adversarial scripts that trigger Cenotaph flaws under Rule R45.
  </p>
  <VectorsTable category="cenotaph" caption="Cenotaph Vectors (C1 through C14)" />

  <h2 id="non-runestone">4. Non-Runestone Outputs (N1–N2)</h2>
  <p>
    These scripts do not begin with the protocol identifier <code>OP_RETURN OP_13</code> and are therefore skipped by indexers without triggering a cenotaph.
  </p>
  <VectorsTable category="non-runestone" caption="Non-Runestone Outputs (N1 through N2)" />

  <h2 id="ignored">5. Ignored Values & Edge Cases</h2>
  <p>
    Under Rule R16, unrecognized odd tags are ignored silently without producing a cenotaph. For example, tag 1 with divisibility &gt; 38 is ignored, defaulting divisibility to 0.
  </p>

  <h2 id="beyond">6. Beyond the Payload</h2>
  <p>
    Some protocol rules depend on chain state and transaction structure outside the OP_RETURN script itself:
  </p>
  <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
    <li><strong>Output Count Bounds:</strong> Edict output indices and pointer index must be strictly less than transaction output count.</li>
    <li><strong>Commitment Maturity:</strong> Etching commitment must have at least 6 confirmations.</li>
    <li><strong>Name Length at Height:</strong> Name must meet the minimum letter length for the block height.</li>
  </ul>

  <FeedbackWidget pageTitle="Runes Test Vectors" />
</BaseLayout>
